{
  "what": "What each in-game check exercises beyond its test-table reads and file (rerun_relation.py; root CLAUDE.md, After a change, only the checks that the change touches run again). Declared by item RIMMANDRAKE_DECLARE_PYRE_CHECKS_CSHARP_SO_TEN_RERUN_NOT_FORTY from each check's chain (validation.py, walk_small_live.py, firehawk_rewards_live.py, wind_burn_live.py, gate_live_proof.py, firefoam_aim_live_proof.py) and the mod's source. A list names the code that produces or changes what the check reads, and the code its scene drives. F.cs::Type,member names parts of a file; F.cs::~ is the members of F.cs that the check's other declared C# names (settings, tuning, kernels). The fire tick's patch (burn stamp, scar ash, fruit) is named by the checks that read ash laid by fire, fruit, burn stamps or fertility, regrowth, or how far a fire spreads; a check that uses fire only as a lure or a hazard (fire-hawk, ashwallow, fire sense, sprayer, herd) does not name it. P_mapgen_log reads the log of the whole load, so it is the whole mod. sc_flamefang_venom is vanilla hediffs on XML defs: no C# of the mod. left_out names what a check's scene names and its entry leaves out on purpose, each with its reason (design/specs/2026-11-24-declaration-check/boundary.md; `declaration_check.py --mod Pyrelands` reads the two against the scenes; item RIMMANDRAKE_CATCH_WRONG_CHECK_DECLARATION_FOUR_PLANTS_MISSED).",
